      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    import math\n\n    # Define variables and values (in millions, except rates and time)\n    assets = 150\n    debt = 100\n    risk_free_rate = 0.05\n    asset_volatility = 0.20\n    time_to_maturity = 3\n\n    # Calculate equity as a call option on the company's assets\n    d1 = (\n        math.log(assets / debt)\n        + (risk_free_rate + 0.5 * asset_volatility**2) * time_to_maturity\n    ) / (asset_volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_maturity))\n    d2 = d1 - asset_volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_maturity)\n\n    normal_cdf = lambda x: 0.5 * (1 + math.erf(x / math.sqrt(2)))\n    equity_value = (\n        assets * normal_cdf(d1)\n        - debt * math.exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_maturity) * normal_cdf(d2)\n    )\n\n    # Return the value in million dollars, rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(equity_value, 2)\n```",
